A channel is a typed communication mechanism between goroutines.

ch := make(chan int)

ch <- 10       // send
x := <-ch      // receive
close(ch)      // close

Unbuffered channels
An unbuffered channel provides direct synchronization between sender and receiver.
The send blocks until a receiver is ready, and the receive blocks until a sender is ready.

Buffered channels
ch := make(chan int, 3)
- capacity is 3

- Receiver gets blocked if the channel buffer is empty and no sender can provide a value.
- Sender gets blocked if the channel buffer is full and no receiver frees up space.

Directional channels
- chan int (Bi-directional)
- chan<- int (Send only)
- <-chan int (Receive only)
- Go channels are bidirectional by default,
  but we can use directional channel types—chan<- for send-only and <-chan for receive-only—to clearly define producer and consumer responsibilities.
